# Schemathesis fuzz-gate ignore-list (issue #369).
#
# The Schemathesis workflow (schemathesis.yml) derives request cases from
# backend/openapi.yaml and gates on two failure classes — 5xx responses
# (`not_a_server_error`, JUnit title "Server error") and auth-protected
# operations that return data without auth (`ignored_auth`, JUnit titles
# "API accepts requests without/invalid authentication") — enforced by
# backend/cmd/schemagate, in the same "ignore-list with justification" shape
# as docker/cis-hardening.ignore. The anonymous pass runs both checks; the
# authenticated pass runs only not_a_server_error (ignored_auth is meaningless
# with real credentials and would false-flag).
#
# Format: one rule per line,
#
#   <kind> <operation-regex>   # justification
#
# where <kind> is one of `server_error` (a 5xx), `auth` (an ignored-auth
# finding), or `*` (both), and <operation-regex> is a Go regexp matched against
# the JUnit testcase name — the Schemathesis operation label (`METHOD /path`,
# e.g. `POST /contacts/import/upload`). A `#` begins a comment; a trailing
# comment on a rule is its justification and is logged on every [ACCEPT].
#
# Every entry must carry a justification — an accepted finding is a written-down
# decision, not a silenced one. Re-run the gate locally before adding an entry:
# the finding must be reproducible, understood, and genuinely out of the gate's
# scope.
#
# No entries at present. The 46 malformed-path-ID / integration / fuzzed-param
# 500s the first fuzz pass surfaced (issue #524) are fixed — see that issue's
# closing commit(s) for the fix and the local Schemathesis re-run that
# confirmed a clean gate before the rules below were removed.
